{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>Say to the priests.</b> After He warned Israel and the sons of Aaron among them, that they be holy, He warned the sons of Aaron that they are obligated to guard against other things, because they are the ministers of HaShem. And it is possible that the meaning of \"say to the priests\" is the entire passage mentioned, for the Torah is in their hands." "<b>And say to them.</b> The reasons for the commandments, which they are obligated to observe separately." "<b>For a soul.</b> It is the dead person." "The word <b>יטמא</b> is from the binyan hithpa'el, and the dagesh in the tet is for the assimilation of the tav." "And the meaning of <b>among his people</b> is among all Israel, who are His people."], :book :leviticus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:11:28.710093112Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}